# Git attributes per path. Only the files below need a rule; every other file follows Git's defaults and the core.autocrlf setting
# of the machine that checks it out.

# The extraction script is kept byte for byte as it was run (tools/README.md gives its SHA-256): no line-ending conversion.
tools/extract_normal_pcap.py -text

# The git hooks are shell scripts: always LF, also on a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true (a CR breaks the shell).
.githooks/* text eol=lf
